<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $94.8 mln May 6.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $94.8 mln May 6.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $94.8 million deficit on May 6 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 6</p>
<p>Exports: $206.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $252 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $206.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $256.1 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $94.8 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $615.1 million</p>
<p>Imports: $678.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $696.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $679.9 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $46.7 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
